flowchart TD
  hook[Existing tasks.script / check hook] --> lock[Native per-behavior group lock covers run and cleanup]
  lock --> mode{Which reset?}
  mode -->|reset, verify with no usable ready copies| inventory
  mode -->|reset --from-ready, no usable copies| build
  mode -->|verify or reset --from-ready, usable copies| fastInventory

  subgraph full[Full build, about 230 s]
    inventory[Pin candidate and inventory owned / unrelated resources] --> release[Validate every owned resource then scoped release]
    release --> snapshot[Export pinned source to disposable checkout]
    snapshot --> prepare[Harness reserve / boot / mount; offline owned Gateway resize to 2560MiB and 2 vCPUs, boot and wait for agent; not ready]
    prepare --> fixture[Shared fixture bootstrap: WireGuard network with the outer VM as operator, Swamp then Gateway, canonical firewall baseline, trust, observers, projection queue and boot fixes]
    fixture --> operator[Native step: the outer VM becomes the operator: nested-CLI wrapper, one profile, WireGuard tunnel]
    operator --> transport[Native step: authenticated operator HTTP and queued worker SSH probe]
    transport --> facts[Native step: one-shot fresh host / ufw / units observation; fail closed if missing]
    facts --> readiness[Native step: scoped Doctor and firewall baseline]
  end

  build[Full build, then make ready copies] --> inventory
  readiness -. after a build-ready run .-> makeReady

  subgraph ready[Ready copies, about 75 s to a checked fleet; the boot is about 50 s of it]
    makeReady[Make ready copies: copy the shared source onto the Gateway and app-dev disks, stop the 3 guests, make them stateful while stopped, copy each without snapshots to fleet-ready-ROLE, drop the generation labels and NIC, record MAC, IP, subnet and Node ids, start the originals] --> readyCheck[Same readiness steps as a build]
    fastInventory[Pin candidate and inventory] --> fastSnapshot[Export pinned source to a new generation; carry the lease and the Gateway runtime state from the previous one; activate last]
    fastSnapshot --> restore[Per guest: delete, copy from ready copy without snapshots, make it stateful if the copy is not yet, label for this attempt, add NIC with saved MAC and IP; start all. No source share: each guest keeps its own checkout]
    restore --> sync[Sync the exported source into the checkout of the Gateway and app-dev by rsync, in parallel; leave out .git, vendor, node_modules, .env, storage, bootstrap/cache]
    sync --> lock{composer.lock changed?}
    lock -->|yes| composer[composer install where it changed]
    lock -->|no| candidate
    composer --> candidate[Candidate overlay in the Gateway: Caddy access, package discovery, migrations, Swamp repository, restart the 2 proof services]
    candidate --> wait[Blocking commands: incus wait agent, systemctl start of the units; tunnel handshake]
    wait --> fastOperator[Native step: operator, pins the restored CA]
    fastOperator --> fastTransport[One readiness check: every Node agent online, Swamp worker enrolled, Gateway knows the operator, Doctor has no finding, record the case baseline]
    fastTransport --> takeBase
    readyCheck --> takeBase[Take base: incus snapshot create base --stateful --reuse on the 3 guests in parallel, about 19 s; the guests keep running; a guest that is not stateful fails here]
  end

  subgraph baseRestore[Restore base, workflow proof-fleet-base-restore, one 30 s limit]
    restoreBase[Restore base on the 3 guests in parallel: incus snapshot restore base --stateful, about 9 s] --> baseAgent[Per guest in parallel: incus wait agent, then set the guest clock from the outer VM, because a restore puts it back to snapshot time]
    restoreBase --> baseTunnel[Beside that: one blocking ping to the nested Gateway; the outer VM tunnel has no valid session, so WireGuard starts a new handshake 15 s after the first unanswered packet]
    baseAgent --> baseStatus[Gateway status is ok]
    baseTunnel --> baseStatus
    baseStatus --> baseAgents[Read node:list until every Node agent is online: the Gateway counts a heartbeat of the last 15 s and they come every 5 s]
    baseAgents --> baseDoctor[Doctor is healthy: it runs last because a silent agent is drift]
    baseDoctor --> baseResult[Healthy, about 20 s, about 26 s after an idle period]
    restoreBase -. error or past 30 s .-> baseFail[Infrastructure error, no retry]
    baseAgent -. error or past 30 s .-> baseFail
    baseTunnel -. error or past 30 s .-> baseFail
    baseStatus -. error or past 30 s .-> baseFail
    baseAgents -. error or past 30 s .-> baseFail
    baseDoctor -. error or past 30 s .-> baseFail
  end

  takeBase -.-> restoreBase
  readiness --> result[Publish generation, readiness and preservation evidence]
  takeBase --> result
  takeBase -. after make-ready .-> receipt
  result --> cases{Verification run?}
  result -. in parallel .-> prune[Keep the active and the previous generation source; delete the others]
  cases -->|yes| commands[Run each case program in order against the one fleet within the case budget; scoped case cleanup]
  cases -->|no| held[Keep generation for explicit test use]
  commands --> baseline[After each case compare its own pre-case database and firewall state; residue fails that case]
  baseline --> receipt[Record a verdict per case; release group lock]
  held --> receipt
  prepare -. failure .-> diagnose[Retain bounded nonsecret diagnostics; timeouts do not skip release]
  fixture -. failure .-> diagnose
  operator -. failure .-> diagnose
  transport -. failure .-> diagnose
  facts -. failure .-> diagnose
  readiness -. failure .-> diagnose
  restore -. failure .-> diagnose
  wait -. failure .-> diagnose
  sync -. failure .-> diagnose
  candidate -. failure .-> diagnose
  fastTransport -. failure .-> diagnose
  takeBase -. failure .-> diagnose
  diagnose --> ownedCleanup[Release only this generation; preserve failure; ready copies stay but are unusable until the next build]
  ownedCleanup --> receipt
